<title>UK: Amstrad, Pace up on digital TV hopes.</title>
<headline>Amstrad, Pace up on digital TV hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Amstrad Plc and Pace Micro Plc rose on Monday on a report that they were among six companies likely to be shortlisted to supply decoder boxes for digital television to British Sky Broadcasting Group Plc .</p>
<p>Separately a Sunday Telegraph report said Amstrad ended a feud with Dixons Plc and had resumed supplying goods to the electrical retailer.</p>
<p>Amstrad shares were up 6-1/2p at 155 by 0928 GMT and Pace was up 7-1/2p at 226.  </p>
<p>A report in the Financial Times said BSkyB was expected to decide to push ahead with digital satellite plans and order about one million decoder boxes worth more than 200 million stg.</p>
<p>No one at Amstrad was available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
